### Client-only shopping authorization checks
### Replace the sample company/item IDs and tokens before testing.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api
@companyId = 1
@itemId = 1
@clientToken = PLACE_CLIENT_JWT_HERE
@staffToken = PLACE_OWNER_OR_MANAGER_OR_EMPLOYEE_JWT_HERE

### Client: expected HTTP 200 (a standalone CLIENT without a company role)
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### Client: expected HTTP 200, assuming item and stock exist
PUT {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/cart/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":1}

### Client: expected HTTP 201, with items in the cart
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{clientToken}}

### Staff or Owner: expected HTTP 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Staff or Owner: expected HTTP 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/cart/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":1}

### Staff or Owner: expected HTTP 403 (no order or stock change)
POST {{baseUrl}}/companies/{{companyId}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
